==German==

===Etymology===
Compound of [[Tinte]] "[[ink]]" and  [[Fisch]]  "[[fish]]".
Attested from the 19th century. 
Glossed as synonym with ''[[Octopus]]'' in  ''Globus'' vol. 61 (1892), [http://books.google.com/books?id=qKDlAAAAMAAJ&q=Tintenfisch&dq=Tintenfisch&hl=en&ei=w7o1TOXnI4OlOOOGlbEE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CDcQ6AEwBA p. 195].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɪntn̩ˌfɪʃ/|/ˈtɪntənˌfɪʃ/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=m|genitive=Tintenfischs|genitive2=Tintenfisches|plural=Tintenfische}}

# any member of the [[Coleoidea]] genus of cephalopods; more specifically of [[cuttlefish]], but also of species of [[octopus|octopus]], [[squid]] etc.

